WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:00.376 --> 00:00:03.462
[dramatic music playing]

2
00:00:11.887 --> 00:00:13.055
[gasps]

3
00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:15.224
[groaning] Mercy!

4
00:00:15.307 --> 00:00:17.435
[yelping]

5
00:00:17.518 --> 00:00:21.272
[groans and grunts]

6
00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.733
[gasps. whimpers]

7
00:00:23.816 --> 00:00:28.195
[grunting and groaning]

8
00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:31.490
[whimpering]

9
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.076
[gasps]

10
00:00:34.702 --> 00:00:36.162
[screams]

11
00:00:37.538 --> 00:00:40.082
[theme music playing]

12
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.074
-== [ www.OpenSubtitles.com ] ==-

13
00:01:09.779 --> 00:01:11.781
[dramatic music playing]

14
00:01:15.117 --> 00:01:16.994
[reporter] Make way. boys!
Comin' through!

15
00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.496
Hey Commish. how about a picture?

16
00:01:18.954 --> 00:01:21.874
We're still waitin' on the coroner.
but cause of death seems pretty obvious.

17
00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:24.627
[tense music playing]

18
00:01:25.377 --> 00:01:26.545
Who's the victim?

19
00:01:26.629 --> 00:01:30.841
Small time second-story man working
his way up to cat burglar apparently.

20
00:01:30.925 --> 00:01:35.012
Looks like he was in the middle of a job
when someone decided to stake his claim.

21
00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.681
Well. did that thief take something
particularly valuable?

22
00:01:37.765 --> 00:01:39.850
We're waiting on a list
from the museum director.

23
00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:42.895
Not to imply that some crimes are
more important than others.

24
00:01:42.978 --> 00:01:47.274
but it's a quarter to five in the morning.
Why am I out of bed. detective?

25
00:01:47.358 --> 00:01:49.068
Because of this.

26
00:01:49.151 --> 00:01:51.195
[dramatic music playing]

27
00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:54.073
-[camera snaps]
-[laughs] That's the ticket. baby!

28
00:01:54.156 --> 00:01:57.493
Front page all the way. [chuckling]

29
00:01:58.077 --> 00:01:59.203
Damn it.

30
00:02:00.246 --> 00:02:03.082
[Hattie. over TV]
I don't know about you. dear viewer.

31
00:02:03.165 --> 00:02:07.002
some in Gotham call
the so-called “Batman” a hero.

32
00:02:07.086 --> 00:02:10.297
But I ask you. does a hero commit murder?

33
00:02:10.381 --> 00:02:12.967
Or sign his name in his victim's blood?

34
00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:16.804
Mothers. has the Batman
made your children safer?

35
00:02:16.887 --> 00:02:22.309
Or do his exploits inspire nightmares
that cause them to wake up screaming?

36
00:02:22.393 --> 00:02:24.812
Who appointed this anonymous vigilante

37
00:02:24.895 --> 00:02:29.108
judge. jury. and executioner
of Gotham's private citizens?

38
00:02:29.191 --> 00:02:32.945
Who will his “justice” condemn next?

39
00:02:33.028 --> 00:02:35.573
And where is the police department?

40
00:02:35.656 --> 00:02:38.117
[Lucius] Bruce. Bruce?

41
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.579
Hello? Paging Mr. Wayne.

42
00:02:41.662 --> 00:02:43.664
-Hm?
-Contracts?

43
00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:47.501
Signatures? You're the one who pushed
all this into one meeting.

44
00:02:47.585 --> 00:02:49.795
Of course. sorry. She just...

45
00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:53.799
She's just doing her job.
keeping your eyes on her.

46
00:02:53.883 --> 00:02:55.175
But it's just fluff.

47
00:02:55.259 --> 00:02:59.263
Or does Commissioner Gordon have
an assassin in his little black book?

48
00:02:59.346 --> 00:03:01.849
Also. the Batman is not an assassin.

49
00:03:01.932 --> 00:03:04.643
You don't agree with her about him?

50
00:03:04.727 --> 00:03:08.272
The guy saved my life once.
so no. I don't.

51
00:03:08.355 --> 00:03:10.649
If there's one thing I know.
it's how to spot a friend.

52
00:03:12.318 --> 00:03:15.446
The truth is. today.
I don't care about anything

53
00:03:15.529 --> 00:03:17.740
that doesn't get
these contracts out the door.

54
00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.035
Did your tax dollars
pay for Rupert Thorne.

55
00:03:21.118 --> 00:03:24.579
and his poor. innocent little boy.
Matthew. to disappear?

56
00:03:24.663 --> 00:03:30.085
No one's seen them since the trial.
Curiouser and curiouser.

57
00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.052
Goodnight. Gotham. Sweet dreams.

58
00:03:38.135 --> 00:03:40.930
[director] And cut. That's a wrap.

59
00:03:41.472 --> 00:03:44.391
-Great show. Hattie.
-Someone bring me a drink!

60
00:03:47.811 --> 00:03:49.980
-I said a drink!
-[groans]

61
00:03:50.773 --> 00:03:51.774
[whimpering]

62
00:03:51.857 --> 00:03:54.401
Ever since that pinko
took us off the gold standard.

63
00:03:54.485 --> 00:03:56.278
the whole country's gone to pot!

64
00:03:56.362 --> 00:03:58.238
One Manhattan. straight up.

65
00:03:58.322 --> 00:04:00.824
I've owned the Batman beat for weeks!

66
00:04:00.908 --> 00:04:04.411
How am I getting scooped
by the Gotham Gazette?

67
00:04:04.495 --> 00:04:05.913
We're an evening program.

68
00:04:05.996 --> 00:04:08.999
Can't beat the morning paper
when a story breaks overnight.

69
00:04:09.083 --> 00:04:12.378
No excuses. I want solutions!

70
00:04:12.461 --> 00:04:17.007
With the papers flogging the Batman.
the people will want feel good stories.

71
00:04:17.091 --> 00:04:19.301
Give them that. and they'll flock to you.

72
00:04:19.385 --> 00:04:24.181
The people are mindless sheep
who want what I tell them to want.

73
00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:27.017
And what I want
is the Batman on my show!

74
00:04:27.101 --> 00:04:29.436
Track him down. and get him in here!

75
00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.313
What about Commissioner Gordon?

76
00:04:31.397 --> 00:04:33.774
Put Gordon in the hot seat.

77
00:04:33.857 --> 00:04:38.737
Force him to explain why his Keystone Kops
can't track down a man in a bat costume.

78
00:04:38.821 --> 00:04:41.490
[satisfied chuckle] Not bad.
Make it happen!

79
00:04:41.573 --> 00:04:43.242
Your wish is my command.

80
00:04:43.325 --> 00:04:45.744
You bet your ass it is!

81
00:04:51.125 --> 00:04:53.127
[suspenseful music playing]

82
00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.962
[tires screeching]

83
00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:00.009
[music intensifies]

84
00:05:05.014 --> 00:05:07.474
[dramatic music playing]

85
00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:13.981
[Mad Monk] Last night.
I sent you on a retrieval mission.

86
00:05:14.064 --> 00:05:19.903
Instead. you commit murder.
Explain yourselves!

87
00:05:21.572 --> 00:05:24.867
We couldn't risk that burglar
taking the artifacts you sent us for!

88
00:05:25.951 --> 00:05:27.619
Show me.

89
00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.166
[man] We found them.
Just as you said we would.

90
00:05:32.249 --> 00:05:37.337
-Plus more treasure for our lord.
-You have done well.

91
00:05:37.421 --> 00:05:42.217
But these? Silverware and baubles?

92
00:05:42.301 --> 00:05:45.179
These are not worthy of Barbatos!

93
00:05:46.638 --> 00:05:48.348
It was the best there was.

94
00:05:48.432 --> 00:05:50.433
I... see.

95
00:05:51.268 --> 00:05:53.604
It is a sign.

96
00:05:54.229 --> 00:06:00.736
Barbatos placed that man in your path
because he requires a new treasure.

97
00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:05.824
He needs blood to fuel his rise!

98
00:06:05.908 --> 00:06:09.036
You are certain? His time is near?

99
00:06:09.119 --> 00:06:11.455
All the wealth you have given him.

100
00:06:11.538 --> 00:06:15.501
all you own
and what the city has tithed...

101
00:06:15.584 --> 00:06:20.839
When he rises.
it will be returned to you ten-fold!

102
00:06:23.175 --> 00:06:28.514
While fire rains down from
his mighty wings upon the unbelievers.

103
00:06:28.597 --> 00:06:33.393
you will be rewarded beyond
your wildest dreams!

104
00:06:33.977 --> 00:06:36.772
Do not falter my children.

105
00:06:36.855 --> 00:06:41.235
Only the worthy
will see his glorious rise!

106
00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:45.280
All hail Barbatos!

107
00:06:46.365 --> 00:06:48.450
[group chanting] All hail Barbatos!

108
00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:50.786
All hail Barbatos!

109
00:06:51.453 --> 00:06:53.413
All hail Barbatos!

110
00:06:55.207 --> 00:06:56.834
[no audible dialogue]

111
00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.922
Any progress on our cat burglar?

112
00:07:02.005 --> 00:07:04.633
Multiple assailants. no traceable weapon.

113
00:07:04.716 --> 00:07:07.427
Looks like the poor bastard got beat.
then stabbed.

114
00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:10.472
Was that Hattie Tetch's producer?

115
00:07:13.892 --> 00:07:15.769
My office. detective.

116
00:07:15.853 --> 00:07:19.064
I'm gonna be a guest
on Hattie's Tea Party tomorrow night.

117
00:07:19.148 --> 00:07:23.485
Sir. it'll be a hit job!
Who put you up to this? The mayor?

118
00:07:23.569 --> 00:07:28.532
No. Ms. Landry approached me directly.
And I agreed it was a good idea.

119
00:07:28.615 --> 00:07:30.701
For you to publicly defend the Batman?

120
00:07:30.784 --> 00:07:33.078
Hattie can say what she likes
about the Batman.

121
00:07:33.162 --> 00:07:34.454
Or me for that matter.

122
00:07:34.538 --> 00:07:37.374
But I won't let her go after the GCPD.

123
00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:40.169
If we're going to build this
into a department to be proud of.

124
00:07:40.252 --> 00:07:43.589
officers on the street have to see
the top brass have their backs.

125
00:07:45.465 --> 00:07:49.052
-Don't worry. I've survived worse.
-You're sure about that?

126
00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:51.263
As you were. detective.

127
00:07:53.015 --> 00:07:54.850
[dramatic music playing]

128
00:07:56.935 --> 00:08:02.357
I'm sure Hattie would prefer
to have you on... if you want my slot.

129
00:08:02.441 --> 00:08:05.944
Whoever drew a bat in that man's blood.
it wasn't me.

130
00:08:06.028 --> 00:08:08.405
I know. Not your style.

131
00:08:08.822 --> 00:08:12.201
Plus to my knowledge.
you don't kill people. Yet.

132
00:08:12.284 --> 00:08:13.577
Even more to the point.

133
00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.871
the coroner confirms our victim
was assaulted

134
00:08:15.954 --> 00:08:18.582
by at least three different individuals.

135
00:08:18.665 --> 00:08:19.917
You...

136
00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:23.670
always work alone.

137
00:08:23.754 --> 00:08:25.214
[sighs]

138
00:08:25.297 --> 00:08:27.049
[dramatic music continues]

139
00:08:27.841 --> 00:08:31.428
[man panting] Help! Help!

140
00:08:32.346 --> 00:08:33.388
[grunting]

141
00:08:36.058 --> 00:08:38.059
[panting continues]

142
00:08:41.395 --> 00:08:43.857
[grunts. groans]

143
00:08:45.776 --> 00:08:47.527
[whimpering]

144
00:08:50.322 --> 00:08:52.658
[group chanting] All hail Barbatos!

145
00:08:52.741 --> 00:08:55.077
-[chanting continues]
-[suspenseful music playing]

146
00:08:55.619 --> 00:08:57.120
[yelps. groans]

147
00:08:57.204 --> 00:08:58.956
Peace. avatar!

148
00:08:59.039 --> 00:09:01.917
We seek your blood. not your death!

149
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.670
A final sacrifice to Barbatos.

150
00:09:04.753 --> 00:09:07.631
It will bring his glorious rise.
so the worthy may--

151
00:09:07.714 --> 00:09:09.091
[grunts]

152
00:09:13.804 --> 00:09:15.305
[grunts]

153
00:09:15.389 --> 00:09:17.182
[smoke hissing]

154
00:09:18.392 --> 00:09:20.060
[suspenseful music continues]

155
00:09:20.852 --> 00:09:23.772
[fighting grunts and groans]

156
00:09:24.356 --> 00:09:25.399
[pained gasp]

157
00:09:25.857 --> 00:09:27.693
[groans and grunts continue]

158
00:09:37.744 --> 00:09:38.912
[gasps]

159
00:09:48.755 --> 00:09:52.217
They say imitation
is the sincerest form of flattery.

160
00:09:52.301 --> 00:09:54.761
I take it you will be confronting
these assailants

161
00:09:54.845 --> 00:09:56.888
to make your feelings
on the matter clear.

162
00:09:56.972 --> 00:09:59.141
I would be now
if I knew where to find them.

163
00:09:59.224 --> 00:10:02.144
Hmm... When you say they vanished.

164
00:10:02.227 --> 00:10:04.229
was that figuratively or literally?

165
00:10:04.313 --> 00:10:07.649
These were humans. not ghosts.
Some kind of cult.

166
00:10:07.733 --> 00:10:09.109
Or the occult.

167
00:10:09.776 --> 00:10:12.738
If only we knew an expert
in such things...

168
00:10:12.821 --> 00:10:14.573
[car engine running]

169
00:10:14.656 --> 00:10:17.117
[jazz music playing]

170
00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:22.622
[jazz music continues]

171
00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.378
[both gasp]

172
00:10:33.216 --> 00:10:34.551
Run along...

173
00:10:34.634 --> 00:10:36.470
I have business to take care of.

174
00:10:36.553 --> 00:10:37.804
I'll be there soon.

175
00:10:39.931 --> 00:10:44.728
I assume you are here about the dead thief
and the bloody bat symbol.

176
00:10:44.811 --> 00:10:47.105
What do you know about Barbatos?

177
00:10:47.189 --> 00:10:49.441
-Barbatos?
-[guitar music playing]

178
00:10:49.524 --> 00:10:51.234
[sighs] I need a drink.

179
00:10:52.903 --> 00:10:56.031
Barbatos is a demon bat god.

180
00:10:56.114 --> 00:10:58.617
who slumbers beneath Gotham City

181
00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:03.580
until his followers sacrifice
sufficient treasure to summon him.

182
00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:07.334
At which point he will rise.
destroy the unbelievers.

183
00:11:07.417 --> 00:11:12.047
and reward his followers
with wealth beyond their wildest dreams.

184
00:11:13.006 --> 00:11:14.841
How do I stop him?

185
00:11:14.925 --> 00:11:16.468
You can't.

186
00:11:16.885 --> 00:11:18.303
He doesn't exist.

187
00:11:20.222 --> 00:11:24.601
Barbatos is an urban myth.
Pops up every few decades or so.

188
00:11:24.684 --> 00:11:28.522
I was just attacked by cultists
who called me his avatar.

189
00:11:28.605 --> 00:11:31.691
You thought a cult
devoted to an evil bat god

190
00:11:31.775 --> 00:11:34.611
wasn't going to weave you
into their mythology? [chuckles]

191
00:11:34.694 --> 00:11:36.029
That's adorable.

192
00:11:37.572 --> 00:11:38.865
This isn't about you.

193
00:11:39.282 --> 00:11:41.201
People like to believe in things.

194
00:11:41.284 --> 00:11:44.079
God. government. capitalism.

195
00:11:44.162 --> 00:11:46.164
Why not Barbatos?

196
00:11:46.248 --> 00:11:48.333
It's so cliché. it'd be funny...

197
00:11:48.875 --> 00:11:50.210
except...

198
00:11:51.336 --> 00:11:52.170
What?

199
00:11:53.755 --> 00:11:55.590
When treasure doesn't do the job.

200
00:11:55.674 --> 00:11:59.719
the cult decides raising Barbatos
requires human sacrifice.

201
00:11:59.803 --> 00:12:02.681
And these cultists
have already killed at least once.

202
00:12:02.764 --> 00:12:06.810
Sounds like something their avatar
should put a stop to. Doesn't it?

203
00:12:06.893 --> 00:12:07.853
Eh?

204
00:12:10.605 --> 00:12:11.982
[dramatic music playing]

205
00:12:12.065 --> 00:12:14.317
So. just before we go live--

206
00:12:14.401 --> 00:12:17.279
Don't you dare touch him with your paints!

207
00:12:17.362 --> 00:12:21.032
The Commissioner's rugged features
need no enhancement.

208
00:12:21.116 --> 00:12:23.660
Good evening. Hattie.
You're in early tonight.

209
00:12:23.743 --> 00:12:26.079
How are you. Commissioner?

210
00:12:26.163 --> 00:12:29.541
Do you need water?
Juice? Something stronger?

211
00:12:29.624 --> 00:12:32.335
Never touch the stuff
before an enemy engagement.

212
00:12:32.419 --> 00:12:33.753
[facetious shock] Enemy?

213
00:12:33.837 --> 00:12:36.465
Well. this is just
a friendly conversation.

214
00:12:36.548 --> 00:12:39.259
It'll be fun!
Make yourself comfortable.

215
00:12:39.342 --> 00:12:43.680
Dala will bring you to set
in two shakes of a lamb's tail. Ta!

216
00:12:44.556 --> 00:12:46.391
[suspenseful music playing]

217
00:12:46.475 --> 00:12:49.603
[Mad Monk]
The avatar's blood calls to its master.

218
00:12:53.482 --> 00:12:55.942
Barbatos is pleased.

219
00:12:56.443 --> 00:12:57.903
[weeping]

220
00:13:00.822 --> 00:13:02.699
What is the matter. my child?

221
00:13:02.782 --> 00:13:05.243
I've followed you for years.

222
00:13:05.327 --> 00:13:08.246
Then tonight. I met the avatar and...

223
00:13:08.788 --> 00:13:10.582
He's not even a believer!

224
00:13:11.166 --> 00:13:13.460
Why would Barbatos choose him?

225
00:13:14.294 --> 00:13:15.462
Hush.

226
00:13:16.254 --> 00:13:19.424
-Have you shared this with the others?
-Not yet.

227
00:13:19.508 --> 00:13:21.551
But my doubts grow.

228
00:13:21.635 --> 00:13:24.012
We've all given so much.

229
00:13:24.095 --> 00:13:26.139
Why does Barbatos not come?

230
00:13:26.932 --> 00:13:30.769
[sighs] Your faith is that shaken.

231
00:13:32.229 --> 00:13:34.648
[weeping] Forgive me.

232
00:13:35.815 --> 00:13:38.401
Then meet our dark lord now.

233
00:13:39.277 --> 00:13:41.154
-[neck snaps]
-[music intensifies]

234
00:13:41.238 --> 00:13:42.155
[body thuds]

235
00:13:42.239 --> 00:13:46.243
And may your sacrifice speed his path.

236
00:13:49.579 --> 00:13:52.499
Any other questions
before your date with destiny?

237
00:13:52.582 --> 00:13:54.501
Just the interview will be enough.
I think.

238
00:13:54.584 --> 00:13:57.963
Good. Humor makes you seem
more approachable.

239
00:13:58.046 --> 00:13:59.631
Just don't try to upstage Hattie.

240
00:13:59.714 --> 00:14:02.759
-[chuckles] I'm sure that's not possible.
-[Hattie] What is this?

241
00:14:02.842 --> 00:14:04.594
-Take your hands off me!
-[gasps]

242
00:14:04.678 --> 00:14:07.180
-Unhand me!
-Stay back!

243
00:14:07.264 --> 00:14:09.641
-[Hattie groaning]
-Police! Don't move!

244
00:14:09.724 --> 00:14:12.227
-[struggling] Let me go!
-Drop the knife.

245
00:14:15.647 --> 00:14:17.440
Good. Now very slowly--

246
00:14:17.524 --> 00:14:18.650
[groans]

247
00:14:20.527 --> 00:14:21.820
[body thuds]

248
00:14:22.654 --> 00:14:24.656
[tense music playing]

249
00:14:25.657 --> 00:14:27.450
Sorry. boss.

250
00:14:28.868 --> 00:14:30.620
You're coming with us.

251
00:14:33.748 --> 00:14:36.501
[dispatcher. over radio]
Attention all units. attention all units.

252
00:14:36.585 --> 00:14:38.628
Kidnapping at Monoscope Pictures.

253
00:14:38.712 --> 00:14:41.172
Commissioner Gordon
and Hattie Tetch are missing.

254
00:14:41.256 --> 00:14:43.383
-[engine revs]
-[tires screech]

255
00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:48.930
A suspect resembling the Batman
was spotted driving away from the scene.

256
00:14:49.014 --> 00:14:52.434
All units be on the alert
for any sign of the Batman.

257
00:14:54.185 --> 00:14:56.855
[Batman] While the police waste their time
looking for the Batman.

258
00:14:56.938 --> 00:14:59.858
the cultists are gonna murder
Gordon and Tetch.

259
00:14:59.941 --> 00:15:01.276
I have to find them.

260
00:15:01.359 --> 00:15:03.361
Unfortunately. there's very little data.

261
00:15:03.445 --> 00:15:06.823
Perhaps if we examine locations
of historic significance to the cult.

262
00:15:06.906 --> 00:15:09.826
No. If this cult thinks I'm their avatar.

263
00:15:09.909 --> 00:15:12.579
they're focused on the present.
not the past.

264
00:15:13.705 --> 00:15:18.335
Midnite said they sacrifice treasure
to Barbatos.

265
00:15:18.418 --> 00:15:23.965
The museum was their first murder.
Maybe it wasn't their first robbery.

266
00:15:24.049 --> 00:15:28.219
I've taken the liberty of compiling data
on the city's recent unsolved crimes.

267
00:15:28.303 --> 00:15:30.013
Perhaps there's a common link.

268
00:15:30.096 --> 00:15:33.642
I'll investigate those locations.
Radio me if you find something.

269
00:15:33.725 --> 00:15:35.810
[suspenseful music playing]

270
00:15:39.064 --> 00:15:40.982
[struggling]

271
00:15:41.066 --> 00:15:42.359
You all right?

272
00:15:42.942 --> 00:15:44.986
Not my first scrap. Gordon.

273
00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:47.739
[chuckles] East Gotham. born and raised.

274
00:15:49.282 --> 00:15:51.534
[music intensifies]

275
00:15:57.123 --> 00:15:58.667
Ungrateful tramp!

276
00:15:59.459 --> 00:16:00.877
You're fired.

277
00:16:01.836 --> 00:16:05.090
You've spent years treating me like dirt.

278
00:16:05.173 --> 00:16:07.509
and I never knew why.

279
00:16:07.592 --> 00:16:09.886
Until I met the monk.

280
00:16:09.969 --> 00:16:14.683
He showed me my suffering
was all part of Barbatos' plan.

281
00:16:14.766 --> 00:16:16.935
You suffer because you're a dirty--

282
00:16:17.018 --> 00:16:19.354
What's this about? Ransom?

283
00:16:19.437 --> 00:16:24.192
Hardly. Barbatos will provide
the worthy with everything they need.

284
00:16:24.275 --> 00:16:26.111
You're going to kill us.

285
00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:29.572
Blood of an ally. blood of an enemy.

286
00:16:29.656 --> 00:16:33.201
You'll be the final sacrifices needed
to summon our lord.

287
00:16:34.703 --> 00:16:36.871
[Batman] What do you have. Pennyworth?

288
00:16:36.955 --> 00:16:39.165
[Pennyworth. over radio]
Based on my triangulations. I've deduced

289
00:16:39.249 --> 00:16:42.043
the most likely lair for those zealots
is St. Bartholomew's Church.

290
00:16:42.127 --> 00:16:44.587
-Good job. Pennyworth.
-[Pennyworth] Thank you. sir.

291
00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:46.172
Godspeed.

292
00:16:46.256 --> 00:16:49.467
-[engine revs]
-[dramatic music playing]

293
00:16:49.551 --> 00:16:54.723
[group chanting] All hail Barbatos!
All hail Barbatos!

294
00:16:54.806 --> 00:16:57.100
All hail Barbatos!

295
00:16:57.183 --> 00:17:01.688
-[chanting continues]
-[unintelligible struggling]

296
00:17:01.771 --> 00:17:04.983
Quiet. No one here cares
what you have to say.

297
00:17:05.066 --> 00:17:08.694
Soon. she will be silent forever. my love.

298
00:17:09.945 --> 00:17:13.282
[moans. kisses]

299
00:17:13.366 --> 00:17:16.703
[dramatic music continues]

300
00:17:22.666 --> 00:17:25.127
Would you care to do the honors?

301
00:17:28.214 --> 00:17:30.800
[group chanting] All hail Barbatos!

302
00:17:30.884 --> 00:17:32.886
All hail Barbatos!

303
00:17:34.888 --> 00:17:35.847
All hail--

304
00:17:37.766 --> 00:17:39.434
[collective gasp]

305
00:17:39.517 --> 00:17:45.023
The avatar has fallen!
Strike him down. my children!

306
00:17:45.106 --> 00:17:46.941
[suspenseful music playing]

307
00:17:50.111 --> 00:17:52.363
[fighting grunts and groans]

308
00:17:59.120 --> 00:17:59.996
Behind you!

309
00:18:07.337 --> 00:18:10.173
[grunts and groans continue]

310
00:18:13.092 --> 00:18:15.053
[struggles. gasps]

311
00:18:15.136 --> 00:18:18.515
No one screws with Hattie Tetch
and gets away with it!

312
00:18:18.598 --> 00:18:20.058
[effort grunts]

313
00:18:33.279 --> 00:18:34.989
[dramatic music playing]

314
00:18:45.875 --> 00:18:50.255
[Mad Monk. echoing] Time for us
to go our separate ways. avatar.

315
00:18:51.005 --> 00:18:54.259
My followers could've killed you
in the park.

316
00:18:54.342 --> 00:18:57.762
I won't be so generous if we meet again.

317
00:18:57.846 --> 00:18:59.639
Turn back now.

318
00:19:00.098 --> 00:19:02.725
The only thing you will find
in these tunnels

319
00:19:02.809 --> 00:19:04.519
is your death.

320
00:19:07.647 --> 00:19:09.315
[dramatic music playing]

321
00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:19.284
-[gun cocks]
-[Mad Monk] I warned you not to chase me.

322
00:19:19.367 --> 00:19:21.327
Hands up. please.

323
00:19:26.165 --> 00:19:28.209
I should thank you.

324
00:19:28.293 --> 00:19:31.880
Convincing people to sacrifice
all their worldly goods to a bat cult

325
00:19:31.963 --> 00:19:34.424
got a lot easier
when you came on the scene.

326
00:19:34.507 --> 00:19:37.844
It was almost enough to make me believe
in Barbatos myself.

327
00:19:40.138 --> 00:19:43.725
I never wanted to get you involved.
Directly.

328
00:19:43.808 --> 00:19:47.478
Alas. cultists tend to get a bit zealous.

329
00:19:47.562 --> 00:19:49.105
I take it as a compliment.

330
00:19:49.188 --> 00:19:53.234
I figured you'd kill them easily
when I sent them to collect your blood.

331
00:19:54.152 --> 00:19:56.863
-Why didn't you?
-I'm no killer.

332
00:19:57.363 --> 00:19:58.740
Ah.

333
00:19:58.823 --> 00:20:02.452
Well. unfortunately for you. I am.

334
00:20:02.535 --> 00:20:03.578
[gun cocks]

335
00:20:04.746 --> 00:20:07.957
[fighting grunts and groans]

336
00:20:13.463 --> 00:20:14.756
[pained groan]

337
00:20:14.839 --> 00:20:15.965
[grunts]

338
00:20:16.049 --> 00:20:16.883
[groans]

339
00:20:21.554 --> 00:20:23.431
[panting] No!

340
00:20:23.514 --> 00:20:24.724
[groaning]

341
00:20:24.807 --> 00:20:29.395
[whimpering] You know. I have a pretty
sweet deal going with this bat cult.

342
00:20:29.479 --> 00:20:31.230
I could cut you in.

343
00:20:33.024 --> 00:20:34.192
[pained grunt]

344
00:20:37.695 --> 00:20:39.447
[dramatic music playing]

345
00:20:50.291 --> 00:20:52.126
Why am I not surprised?

346
00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:55.129
Montoya. let headquarters know
we won't need to track down

347
00:20:55.213 --> 00:20:56.714
the ringleader after all.

348
00:20:58.424 --> 00:21:02.470
Where's my former producer?
I want to fire her again!

349
00:21:02.553 --> 00:21:04.138
Blasphemer!

350
00:21:04.222 --> 00:21:06.391
-[screams]
-[gasps. yelps]

351
00:21:06.474 --> 00:21:08.226
[struggling. gurgling]

352
00:21:08.309 --> 00:21:10.228
[gasping]

353
00:21:11.145 --> 00:21:14.065
Have you come to show us the way. avatar?

354
00:21:14.148 --> 00:21:16.609
Will you bring Barbatos' terrible glory?

355
00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:20.405
No!

356
00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:24.701
All hail Barbatos!
All hail Barbatos!

357
00:21:24.784 --> 00:21:27.078
All hail Barbatos.

358
00:21:27.161 --> 00:21:28.663
All hail Barbatos!

359
00:21:29.622 --> 00:21:32.458
All hail Barbatos.
[crying]

360
00:21:34.836 --> 00:21:39.674
Suffice to say.
last night was quite the adventure.

361
00:21:39.757 --> 00:21:43.761
And I don't mind admitting I wouldn't
be here to tell you all the tale

362
00:21:43.845 --> 00:21:46.305
if not for one man...

363
00:21:46.389 --> 00:21:48.808
Commissioner James Gordon.

364
00:21:48.891 --> 00:21:51.394
I can't take all the credit.
You held your own.

365
00:21:51.477 --> 00:21:53.771
And of course
the Batman's arrival was key.

366
00:21:53.855 --> 00:21:57.650
[laughs] The Batman inspired that lunatic
and his followers

367
00:21:57.734 --> 00:21:59.694
to kidnap us in the first place!

368
00:21:59.777 --> 00:22:03.823
[over TV] Sadly. the world is full
of weak-minded. passive people.

369
00:22:03.906 --> 00:22:05.950
like my former producer.

370
00:22:06.034 --> 00:22:08.828
who are easy prey
for charismatic charlatans.

371
00:22:09.662 --> 00:22:12.707
-Not like you. dear viewer.
-[suspenseful music playing]

372
00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:16.753
You're far too intelligent to fall
for someone like that.

373
00:22:16.836 --> 00:22:18.713
Goodnight. Gotham.

374
00:22:18.796 --> 00:22:19.964
Sweet dreams.

375
00:22:20.048 --> 00:22:22.050
[music sting]

376
00:22:23.634 --> 00:22:25.595
[credits music playing]

376
00:22:26.305 --> 00:23:26.554
